 "response": "**Thaza's budget is now $3123K.**\n\nOnly Finance Office records change the budget, so every message from other teams was ignored.\n\n**Resolving the withdrawals.** Several withdrawals are themselves withdrawn, so I worked each chain back from its last record.\n- **#0007 (+$193K) is withdrawn.** In the chain #0605 \u2192 #0251 \u2192 #0144 \u2192 #0021 \u2192 #0020 \u2192 #0016 \u2192 #0010 \u2192 #0007, #0605 stands, which cancels #0251. With #0251 gone, #0144 stands and cancels #0021. That lets #0020 cancel #0016, so #0010 stands and withdraws #0007.\n- **#0006 (+$518K) stands.** In #1544 \u2192 #0183 \u2192 #0100 \u2192 #0032 \u2192 #0006, #1544 cancels #0183. That leaves #0100 standing, which cancels #0032, the withdrawal of #0006.\n- I resolved every other chain the same way. For example, #0019, #0053, #0105, #0313 and #0287 end up withdrawn. #0009, #0029, #0025, #0064 and #0778 stand.\n\n**Applying the updates.** Starting from $2750K (#0001), I applied every Finance Office increase and decrease that was not withdrawn, in order. Some checkpoints:\n- After #0004 (\u2212594) and #0006 (+518): $2674K\n- After #0120 (+586): $3866K\n- After #0406 (\u2212549) and #0408 (\u2212392): $2521K\n- After #0617 (\u2212563): $2878K\n- After #0778 (\u2212419): $2306K\n- After #1251 (\u2212103): $1663K\n- After #1597 (\u221265), the last update: **$3123K**\n\nThe result rests on one long manual running total, so a single slip would change the figure.\n\nANSWER: $3123K",
